# No Duplicate Implementations

## Purpose

Prevent duplicate components, utilities, services, routes, schemas, hooks, and feature implementations.

## When This Applies

- Creating components
- Creating helper functions
- Adding API clients
- Adding services
- Creating hooks
- Adding pages or routes

## Required Workflow

1. Search for existing implementations before adding a new one.
2. Extend or compose existing code when it fits.
3. Extract shared logic when duplication appears.
4. Delete or consolidate obsolete duplicates only when safe.
5. Document any intentional duplicate with a clear reason.

## Standards

- One responsibility should have one primary implementation.
- Prefer shared primitives over repeated custom variants.
- Keep naming clear so future agents can find the implementation.
- Refactor duplicate logic when it is in the scope of the task.
- Use existing design system and API clients first.

## Do Not

- Do not create ButtonNew, DashboardV2, FinalComponent, or temporary alternate implementations.
- Do not copy paste existing logic into a new file without refactoring.
- Do not leave old dead code after replacement.
- Do not create a second API client for the same backend.
- Do not duplicate validation schemas across frontend and backend when shared types exist.

## Verification Checklist

- The existing project pattern was inspected before changes were made.
- The implementation is scoped to the user request.
- Unsafe files, secrets, and unrelated changes are excluded.
- Applicable lint, typecheck, test, build, or validation commands were run when available.
- Any skipped or failed verification is reported clearly.

## Related Skills

- Use the matching `.cursor/skills/` workflow when one exists for this rule.
- When no matching skill exists, follow this rule directly and keep changes minimal, safe, and verifiable.
